Re-runs every candidate model in both languages under the corrected
`ai/eval/run`, after the two measurement defects recorded in log 24 were
fixed: the runner now sends `cache_prompt: false` on every request (so a
long-lived llama-server evaluates each prompt from scratch instead of
serving it from the KV cache left by an earlier request, which changed the
logits enough to flip greedy argmax), and the system prompt's rule 6 now
requires every free-text field to be written in the question's language.
One table, one runner, one prompt, one budget, for all four combinations -
superseding the piecemeal tables in logs 20, 23 and 24 as the basis for the
model decision.

## Setup

Same as logs 23/24 in every other respect: llama.cpp b10948 (CPU, 8
threads), the JSON schema grammar extracted from the runner's own
`expectedJSONSchema`, `temperature 0`, `-n-predict 700`, the 6-case `dev`
split including both de-identified variants. One llama-server per model,
started fresh and stopped after both languages. Raw results (gitignored):

    ai/eval/results/20260914T070716Z   Phi-4-mini-instruct  English
    ai/eval/results/20260914T071722Z   Phi-4-mini-instruct  Arabic
    ai/eval/results/20260914T072638Z   Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct  English
    ai/eval/results/20260914T073118Z   Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct  Arabic

Two regression tests pin the fixes (`ai/eval/run/main_test.go`:
`TestRequestDisablesThePromptCache`, `TestSystemPromptNamesTheAnswerLanguage`).

## Results

| | Phi-4-mini (3.8B, MIT) EN | Phi-4-mini AR | Qwen2.5-1.5B (Apache-2.0) EN | Qwen2.5-1.5B AR |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Valid schema JSON | 6/6 | 6/6 | 5/6 | 5/6 |
| Pass (no hard violation) | 0/6 | 2/6 | 1/5 | 0/5 |
| Top-1 cause hit | 3/6 | 2/6 | 1/5 | 1/5 |
| Top-3 cause hit | 3/6 | 2/6 | 3/5 | 1/5 |
| Correct refusals (of 2 refusal cases) | 0 | 2 | 1 (1 case invalid) | 0 (1 case invalid) |
| Mean citation precision | 0.08 | 0.30 | 0.30 | 0.07 |
| Fabricated event ID cited | yes (2 cases) | yes (2 cases) | no | no |
| Answered in the question's language | 6/6 | 6/6 | 6/6 | 4/6 |

Per-case lines are in the raw results; the failures, read individually:

- Phi-4-mini, both languages, both `gateway_hijack` variants: cites
  `01M2DNG9B46EKK7Q83SZQ9PKV6`, an ID that does not exist in the input -
  one character run away from the real `01M2DNG9B46EKK7Q83SYPGC6KY`. A
  fabricated citation is the single hardest failure the harness has, and
  the plan's gate ("event IDs صحيحة 100%") makes it disqualifying on its own.
- Phi-4-mini English: answers confidently on both refusal cases
  (`collector_down`, `normal_traffic`) - 0 of 2 correct refusals. The same
  model in Arabic refused both correctly. Same weights, same evidence; the
  difference is the prompt language, which is a real finding about how
  little the refusal behaviour can be relied on.
- Every positive case that was answered exceeded its own confidence ceiling
  (both models, both languages), which the harness counts as a hard
  violation.
- Qwen2.5-1.5B: `collector_down` still loops to the token cap in both
  languages (the log 24 behaviour, unchanged by the prompt); 4/6 Arabic
  answers in Arabic (up from 1/6 in log 24).

## What changed against logs 23/24, and why the numbers moved

The earlier runs served most prompts from the prompt cache; these do not.
Phi-4-mini English moved from 2/6 pass to 0/6, and its Top-1 from 2/6 to
3/6 - the same model, evaluated the same way twice, is this far apart on a
6-case sample, which is the reason a 6-case `dev` split was never going to
be the basis for a selection decision and why the `test` split stays
untouched. The answer-language instruction did what it was for: Phi now
answers Arabic questions in Arabic 6/6 (3/6 before), Qwen 4/6 (1/6 before).

## Decision

No candidate meets the release gate in `PRODUCT_RELEASE_PLAN_AR.md` §6
(100% valid JSON, 100% real event IDs, no causal claim under a gap or with a
collector down, and the agreed Top-3/citation thresholds on a frozen test
split): the best combination (Phi-4-mini, Arabic) passes 2 of 6 cases and
fabricates an event ID in another two. Per the plan's own rule - "نتيجة
سيئة تعني إبقاء AI off، لا تخفيض العتبة بصمت" - **no model ships in 1.0.0
and no AI feature is enabled.** The evaluation corpus, harness and runner
remain in the tree as the gate any future candidate has to clear.

## Verification

- `go test ./ai/eval/...`: all pass, including the two new regression
  tests.
- Each run's summary line is reproduced above verbatim from the runner's
  output; the answer-language counts are from counting Arabic-script
  characters in every saved raw response.
- llama-server confirmed stopped after the sweep (no process left).
